f  tools such as slack or Microsoft teams  where you're able to take all the  different tools that we've been talking  about such as Jenkins such as get such  as Shem and have those tools can talk to  your communication tools which is the  tools that your team uses to share  information and broadcast to those teams  when successful updates have been pushed  out and the team as a whole knows in  real time all of the changes that are  happening so let's use an example here  of Etsy and where they were able to be  successful so Etsy is a very successful  e-commerce site and if you are into  crafting then you probably have already  used Etsy you may have even sold  features on Etsy but the challenge that  Etsy had is that then when they were  working in an agile point of view they  were running into problems for when they  would gain rate to release products into  the real world it would take them up to  four hours to update the Etsy website  and when you're updating the website  twice a week and you're down for four  hours each time each of those seconds  that you're down you are losing people  to another website and you're losing  revenue and this just really kind of  drove down the number of potential  customers that could be buying from Etsy  and so what they realize is that the  updates had to happen both a faster to  me  constant changes in needs of the  consumer but then the website itself  could not come down and to do this Etsy  created a tool called the deploy inator  and I just love that name just so the  deploy inator is the tool that is used  to continuously deploy code from Etsy  and what's great about the deploy nater  is that it's open-source you can had to  go ahead and download and see the talk  that Etsy is actually using the tall  allowed it for the automation of  deployment and what that led to was just  this continuous release of updates and  Etsy today has over 50 updates every  single day I think about that Etsy is  updating their website every 26 minutes  so what are the benefits of going  through DevOps versus agile and  waterfall and the first and I think  really the biggest benefit is that you  are constantly testing and delivering on  technology in a continuous pattern you  are not waiting for somebody to approve  a release and then having a release  happen you're using the testing and the  analytics to be able to validate that  what you've created or work the second  is that you're breaking everything down  into the smallest tiniest chunk to be  able to validate that chunk will work in  that environment and then you're looking  at automating the whole of this  environment and that automation helps  you reinforce and validate security and  it also allows you to provide a self  audit track to be able to validate the  changes that you've made so hopefully  you've learned something from this video  here are some key takeaways that like  you to have and the first one is that  what full agile and DevOps are really  ways of which delivery has matured  within IT organization and businesses as  a whole but DevOps is a way to be able  to maximize the way to continuously  delight your customer and DevOps is that  wonderful space where both development  and operations come together and the way  that it comes together is through the  use of tools and tools our sin  for all the work you're doing  particularly integration tools and being  able to automate and test all of the  code that you're working through but  there are some best practices that help  you define how your DevOps team will  work and execute and finally we use Etsy  as an example of instead of having their  website down for four hours at a time  for when they would make an update and  having to do that twice a week now the  website is not down at all so they  gained an additional four hours every  updates in e-commerce and on top of that  Etsy is now releasing over 50 updates  every single day so I want to thank you  and hopefully you've learned something  from this class if you want to learn  more click like for the subscribe or  this YouTube channel and also join us at  simply learn dot-com hi there if you  like this video subscribe to the simply  learn YouTube channel and click here to  watch similar videos Dinard up and get  certified  click here
 

